  "summary": "The Richmond (CA) City Council voted 4-3 to extend its Flock Safety ALPR contract through the end of 2026 while staff explores alternative vendors and adds stronger guardrails against data-sharing with outside agencies. The cameras have been disabled since October, when RPD discovered federal agencies had access to data via Flock's 'National Lookup' feature.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the Richmond Police Department discovered that federal agencies had access to the data collected through a back-end \"National Lookup\" feature enabled by Flock Safety.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "the council voted 4-3 in favor of extending the contract, with instructions to the city staff to bake in stronger guardrails to prevent any data sharing with outside agencies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "We cannot be trusting a company that tricked you and was not upfront",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
